  "goodToKnow": "Der Ehrenbürger (die Ehrenbürgerin) is an honorary citizen, the highest honour a German city can award. Berlin's list includes Marlene Dietrich, honoured posthumously in 2002, and Mikhail Gorbachev. Some cities have revoked Nazi-era honorary citizenships, such as Hitler's. Ehren- means honorary: der Ehrendoktor, das Ehrenamt (voluntary post). The plural is the same."
